    "intro": "Santa's famous reindeer all have names that sound like movement and light, and any new recruit to the team needs one too. This **reindeer name generator** makes classic sleigh-team names, cute ones for a toy reindeer, and funny ones for the reindeer that always lands on the wrong roof.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Where Santa's reindeer names come from",
        "content": "<p>Santa's reindeer were named in a poem: <em>A Visit from St. Nicholas</em>, better known as <em>'Twas the Night Before Christmas</em>, published in 1823.</p><ul><li><strong>The eight:</strong> Dasher, Dancer, Prancer, Vixen, Comet, Cupid, Donner and Blitzen. The poem first called the last two Dunder and Blixem, Dutch for thunder and lightning.</li><li><strong>Rudolph</strong> came much later, in 1939, when Robert L. May wrote his story for a booklet given away by the Montgomery Ward department store.</li><li><strong>New names</strong> follow the same pattern: speed, light and movement. That's why the classic style has names like Frosthoof and Windlight. The famous nine are left out, so every name is new.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Real reindeer facts",
        "content": "<p>Reindeer are the only deer where both males and females grow antlers.</p><ul><li><strong>Santa's team is probably female:</strong> males drop their antlers in late autumn, while females keep theirs through the winter. A reindeer with antlers on Christmas Eve is most likely a female.</li><li><strong>Same animal, two names:</strong> in North America wild reindeer are called caribou.</li><li><strong>Built for snow:</strong> their hooves spread wide on snow and their noses warm the cold air before it reaches their lungs.</li></ul><p>For the snowman in the garden, try the <a href=\"snowman-name-generator.html\">Snowman Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For the rest of the season, see all the <a href=\"../categories/christmas-names.html\">Christmas name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are Santa's reindeer called?",
        "answer": "Dasher, Dancer, Prancer, Vixen, Comet, Cupid, Donner and Blitzen, from the 1823 poem 'Twas the Night Before Christmas, plus Rudolph, who was added in 1939."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are Santa's reindeer male or female?",
        "answer": "Probably female. Male reindeer shed their antlers in late autumn, but females keep theirs through the winter, so reindeer with antlers at Christmas are most likely female."
